To provide a more complete assessment of the capabilities of topology for SVG identification, we also used our methodology to analyse a spatial transcriptomics data set consisting of samples of multiple physiological zones of the heart from myocardial infarction and control patients (Kuppe et al. 2022). These samples are very different from the kidney samples analysed above in that gene expression is resolved to a much larger number of much smaller wells. These samples contain expression on 16272 genes resolved to between 1890 and 4659 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
